                                The Backup created here can be restored on the same server.','The Backup created here can be migrated to a new server.'=>'The Backup created here can be migrated to a new server.','Migration Status'=>'Migration Status','Hide Notification'=>'Hide Notification','Sure! I\'d love to help'=>'Sure! I\'d love to help','Congrats!'=>'Congrats!','This feature works only with hosts that support cPanel.'=>'This feature works only with hosts that support cPanel.','Duplicator Pro!'=>'Duplicator Pro!','This feature is only availble in '=>'This feature is only availble in ','Create the database and database user at install time without leaving the installer!'=>'Create the database and database user at install time without leaving the installer!','Basic'=>'Basic','Prefills'=>'Prefills','Enabling this option will allow for basic password protection on the installer. Before running the installer the password below must be entered before proceeding with an install.  This password is a general deterrent and should not be substituted for properly keeping your files secure.  Be sure to remove all installer files when the install process is completed.'=>'Enabling this option will allow for basic password protection on the installer. Before running the installer the password below must be entered before proceeding with an install.  This password is a general deterrent and should not be substituted for properly keeping your files secure.  Be sure to remove all installer files when the install process is completed.','Security:'=>'Security:','Enable Password Protection'=>'Enable Password Protection','Security'=>'Security','Branding is a way to customize the installer look and feel.  With branding you can create multiple brands of installers.'=>'Branding is a way to customise the installer look and feel.  With branding you can create multiple brands of installers.','Branding'=>'Branding','All values in this section are OPTIONAL! If you know ahead of time the database input fields the installer will use, then you can optionally enter them here and they will be prefilled at install time.  Otherwise you can just enter them in at install time and ignore all these options in the Installer section.'=>'All values in this section are OPTIONAL! If you know ahead of time the database input fields the installer will use, then you can optionally enter them here and they will be prefilled at install time.  Otherwise you can just enter them in at install time and ignore all these options in the Installer section.','Setup/Prefills'=>'Setup/Prefills','Installer password protection is off'=>'Installer password protection is off','Installer password protection is on'=>'Installer password protection is on','This is an advanced database backwards compatibility feature that should ONLY be used if having problems installing Backups. If the database server version is lower than the version where the Backup was built then these options may help generate a script that is more compliant with the older database server. It is recommended to try each option separately starting with mysql40.'=>'This is an advanced database backwards compatibility feature that should ONLY be used if having problems installing Backups. If the database server version is lower than the version where the Backup was built then these options may help generate a script that is more compliant with the older database server. It is recommended to try each option separately starting with mysql40.','<b>Overview:</b><br> This advanced option excludes all files from the Backup.  Only the database and a copy of the installer.php will be included in the archive.zip file. The option can be used for backing up and moving only the database.'=>'<b>Overview:</b><br> This advanced option excludes all files from the Backup.  Only the database and a copy of the installer.php will be included in the archive.zip file. The option can be used for backing up and moving only the database.','Fail'=>'Fail','Yes. Continue without applying any file filters.'=>'Yes. Continue without applying any file filters.','To apply a "Quick Filter" click the "Add Filters & Rescan" button'=>'To apply a "Quick Filter" click the "Add Filters & Rescan" button','At least one or more checkboxes were checked in "Quick Filters".'=>'At least one or more checkboxes were checked in "Quick Filters".','Do you want to continue?'=>'Do you want to continue?','Input fields not valid'=>'Input fields not valid','Please retry by going to the'=>'Please retry by going to the','An invalid request was made to this page.'=>'An invalid request was made to this page.','upgrade to pro'=>'upgrade to pro','Duplicator does not support WordPress multisite migrations.  We strongly recommend using Duplicator Pro which currently supports full multisite migrations and various other subsite scenarios.'=>'Duplicator does not support WordPress multisite migrations.  We strongly recommend using Duplicator Pro which currently supports full multisite migrations and various other subsite scenarios.','If the scanner is unable to locate the wp-config.php file in the root directory, then you will need to manually copy it to its new location. This check will also look for core WordPress paths that should be included in the Backup for WordPress to work correctly.'=>'If the scanner is unable to locate the wp-config.php file in the root directory, then you will need to manually copy it to its new location. This check will also look for core WordPress paths that should be included in the Backup for WordPress to work correctly.','It is recommended to have a version of WordPress that is greater than %1$s.  Older version of WordPress can lead to migration issues and are a security risk. If possible please update your WordPress site to the latest version.'=>'It is recommended to have a version of WordPress that is greater than %1$s.  Older version of WordPress can lead to migration issues and are a security risk. If possible please update your WordPress site to the latest version.','Timeouts may occur for larger Backups when [max_execution_time] time in the php.ini is too low.  A value of 0 (recommended) indicates that PHP has no time limits. An attempt is made to override this value if the server allows it.'=>'Timeouts may occur for larger Backups when [max_execution_time] time in the php.ini is too low.  A value of 0 (recommended) indicates that PHP has no time limits. An attempt is made to override this value if the server allows it.','If the value is [dynamic] then its possible for PHP to run longer than the default.  If the value is [fixed] then PHP will not be allowed to run longer than the default. <br/><br/> If this value is larger than the [Allowed Runtime] above then the web server has been enabled with a timeout cap and is overriding the PHP max time setting.'=>'If the value is [dynamic] then its possible for PHP to run longer than the default.  If the value is [fixed] then PHP will not be allowed to run longer than the default. <br/><br/> If this value is larger than the [Allowed Runtime] above then the web server has been enabled with a timeout cap and is overriding the PHP max time setting.','This option is available on some hosts that allow for users to adjust server configurations.  With this option you will be directed to an FAQ page that will show various recommendations you can take to improve/unlock constraints set up on this server.'=>'This option is available on some hosts that allow for users to adjust server configurations.  With this option you will be directed to an FAQ page that will show various recommendations you can take to improve/unlock constraints set up on this server.','OPTION 4:'=>'OPTION 4:','Option 4: Configure Server'=>'Option 4: Configure Server',' Overview'=>' Overview','A two-part install minimizes server load and can avoid I/O and CPU issues encountered on some budget hosts. With this procedure you simply build a \'database-only\' Backup, manually move the website files, and then run the installer to complete the process.'=>'A two-part install minimises server load and can avoid I/O and CPU issues encountered on some budget hosts. With this procedure you simply build a \'database-only\' Backup, manually move the website files, and then run the installer to complete the process.','Option 3: Two-Part Install'=>'Option 3: Two-Part Install','On some servers the build will continue to run in the background. To validate if a build is still running; open the \'tmp\' folder above and see if the Backup file is growing in size or check the main Backups screen to see if the Backup completed. If it is not then your server has strict timeout constraints.'=>'On some servers the build will continue to run in the background. To validate if a build is still running; open the \'tmp\' folder above and see if the Backup file is growing in size or check the main Backups screen to see if the Backup completed. If it is not then your server has strict timeout constraints.','Retry Build With Filters'=>'Retry build with filters','For example, you could  filter out the  "/wp-content/uploads/" folder to create the Backup then move the files from that directory over manually.  If this work-flow is not desired or does not work please check-out the other options below.'=>'For example, you could  filter out the  "/wp-content/uploads/" folder to create the Backup then move the files from that directory over manually.  If this work-flow is not desired or does not work please check-out the other options below.','The first pass for reading files on some budget hosts maybe slow and have conflicts with strict timeout settings setup by the hosting provider.  In these cases, it is recommended to retry the build by adding file filters to larger files/directories.'=>'The first pass for reading files on some budget hosts may be slow and have conflicts with strict timeout settings setup by the hosting provider.  In these cases, it is recommended to retry the build by adding file filters to larger files/directories.','Option 2: File Filters'=>'Option 2: File Filters','Build a new Backup using the new engine format.'=>'Build a new Backup using the new engine format.','Enable DupArchive'=>'Enable DupArchive','Go to Duplicator &gt; Settings &gt; Backups Tab &gt; Backup Engine &gt;'=>'Go to Duplicator &gt; Settings &gt; Backups Tab &gt; Backup Engine &gt;','On the scanner step check to make sure your Backup is under 500MB. If not see additional options below.'=>'On the scanner step check to make sure your Backup is under 500MB. If not see additional options below.','Enable the DupArchive format which is specific to Duplicator and designed to perform better on constrained budget hosts.'=>'Enable the DupArchive format which is specific to Duplicator and designed to perform better on constrained budget hosts.','Option 1: DupArchive'=>'Option 1: DupArchive','This may take several minutes to complete.'=>'This may take several minutes to complete.','Keep this window open and do not close during the build process.'=>'Keep this window open and do not close during the build process.','Auto File Filters'=>'Auto File Filters','Auto Directory Filters'=>'Auto Directory Filters','- Switch to the %s which requires a capable hosting provider (VPS recommended).'=>'- Switch to the %s which requires a capable hosting provider (VPS recommended).','ZipArchive Engine'=>'ZipArchive Engine','- In %s consider adding file/directory or database table filters.'=>'- In %s consider adding file/directory or database table filters.','- In the \'Size Checks\' section above consider adding filters (if notice is shown).'=>'- In the \'Size Checks\' section above consider adding filters (if notice is shown).','- Add data filters to get the Backup size under %s: '=>'- Add data filters to get the Backup size under %s: ','Step 1'=>'Step 1','The build can\'t continue because the total size of files and the database exceeds the %s limit that can be processed when creating a DupArchive Backup. '=>'The build can\'t continue because the total size of files and the database exceeds the %s limit that can be processed when creating a DupArchive Backup. ','The total size of the site (files plus  database).'=>'The total size of the site (files plus database).','Total Size:'=>'Total Size:','The notices for tables are %1$s records or names with upper-case characters.  Individual tables will not trigger a notice message, but can help narrow down issues if they occur later on.'=>'The notices for tables are %1$s records or names with upper-case characters.  Individual tables will not trigger a notice message, but can help narrow down issues if they occur later on.','Total size and row counts are approximate values.  The thresholds that trigger notices are %1$s records total for the entire database.  Larger databases take more time to process.  On some budget hosts that have cpu/memory/timeout limits this may cause issues.'=>'Total size and row counts are approximate values.  The thresholds that trigger notices are %1$s records total for the entire database.  Larger databases take more time to process.  On some budget hosts that have cpu/memory/timeout limits this may cause issues.','PHP is unable to read the following items and they will NOT be included in the Backup.  Please work with your host to adjust the permissions or resolve the symbolic-link(s) shown in the lists below.  If these items are not needed then this notice can be ignored.'=>'PHP is unable to read the following items and they will NOT be included in the Backup.  Please work with your host to adjust the permissions or resolve the symbolic-link(s) shown in the lists below.  If these items are not needed then this notice can be ignored.','If this environment/system and the system where it will be installed are set up to support Unicode and long paths then these filters can be ignored.  If you run into issues with creating or installing a Backup, then is recommended to 